A. Persona Perspective Summary

As a patient currently navigating the NHS during winter pressures, I feel deeply anxious and frustrated. Waiting rooms are overcrowded and poorly ventilated, which makes me afraid of catching something else while waiting to be seen. Appointments with my GP feel rushed and impersonal, and the referral process to a specialist seems like a black box where my case disappears for weeks. The care feels fragmented; I have to repeat my story to every new clinician. I don’t feel prioritized as a whole person—rather, I feel like a problem to be processed quickly. My primary concern is whether the current system can deliver safe, coordinated, respectful, and tailored care when I most need it. From my perspective, any improvement must directly address access, waiting times, continuity, emotional burden, and the risk of hospital-acquired infections.

